A||||13||87ECO5||Shocked the pizza guy||||1||
Z||000000||87ECO5||02-19-2000||01:07 AM||||Ordered Cassanos Pizza tonight.  Doorbell rang, I opened the door, saw the pizza guy but ... ooohhhh ... what he drove.  Yep, that's right - a Fiero.<P>I said:  "Heeeyyyy, an '85 GT, right?"  He gave me a long, blank look then realized I was talking about his mode of transportation.<P>We talked for a few minutes.  He mentioned having to dump about $300 bucks last week on it just to do a minor tune-up (sensors, gaskets, etc - I guess the labor hurt him).  Of course, the whole time I'm thinking "man, we could have done all that in my driveway for next to nothing!"<P>We would have talked longer but the wife was yelling something about cold pizza.  "Hey!, put it in the microwave and hush!  There's a Fiero in my driveway and it's not mine!  Umm, sorry honey ... I was just kidding ... yes dear ... umm, love you ..."<P>Sure wish I'd had one of Cliff's "forum cards" to pass along to him.<P>In the words of Fiero Dave ... "Thanks for the space ..."||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||02:03 AM||||My (late) mother-in-law used to work at Cassanos.  If the local pizza person ever showed up at MY door driving a Fiero, I'd have to gently put my arm around my wife and kindly tell her to go fix a bowl of cereal till I got done. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Lance||02-19-2000||02:30 AM||||"Forum Car" Whats that? And where can I get some?||||reg||9
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||02:38 AM||||Here it is.  Save it to disk, then print as many as you need.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcard.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carolina 88GT||02-19-2000||10:15 AM||||Thanks MM.  There are only like 4 other operating fieros in my town (mine includded) and this will be a good way to "indoctrinate" the others.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||10:42 AM||||That's about all there are in my town, too.  A couple of the other Fiero owners aren't what you'd call friendly and the only one that is friendly is a pain (actually that's his nickname-I swear!).  Not a bad selection, though.  '87 coupe, '84 Econo (although he swears that it's an '83!  Just shows what he knows, huh?) and one guy (Pain) has 2 GTs (!).  Ones an '86 (Getrag, hopped up 2.8, custom paint, flames--I'll have to get some pics in the spring), and the other is a bone stock (black) '87 GT (auto, recently added wing, very good shape but never driven and won't sell).<BR>Have I rambled enough? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phaeton||02-19-2000||01:43 PM||||The power of a Fiero. The only Fiero owner I know is a pilot I used to work with, and we can't stand each other (he's an elitist, I'm a hippie), but when we run into each other when driving Fieros, different!  Last time he showed me how to clean the window pads and I pointed out the garage had rotated his tires for him, putting rears on front, causing his lurching.  Politics don't even come up when something as cool as a Fiero is around!<BR>I do an occasional parts run in the Fiero, the reactions are Great, no negative, mostly its 'Wow, they let you drive a Fiero?'<BR>The local Chevy dealer has a new mechanic with a black notchback, but can't get him to even wave, an overly serious fellow IMO.<BR>Monkey, you didn't ramble enough, but that's OK, I filled in. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Carolina 88GT||02-19-2000||02:38 PM||||I just had an experience........Pulled into the local radio store, I want to upgrade the stock radio to one of the pioneer din 1/2 (I dont like radio's that you have to use a kit on, the things jut out from the dash and look crappy)...anyways...the guy walks over to the window and says.."Thats a nice car"..."What is that a Toyota?"..Feeling a little offended by that remark I calmly said "No...its a Pontiac."......He replied with a serious face "Who make Pontiac".  I smiled and walked out of the store.||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||02-19-2000||05:02 PM||||too funny, Carolina!!<P>unfortunately, in greensboro, there aren't many around.  i do see, on a good day, 3 in my business park... one of those is the wragged out 84 se of a guy that works for me.<P>i bet if my car was driveable, i would see more cars!<P>did you have any luck at the bone yard today?<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000009||Carolina 88GT||02-19-2000||05:16 PM||||It dumped down for a bit.  Never got the chance to get out there.  Will try and make a go of it on Monday......may even call in sick just to do it.  Course I probably shouldnt....I already spent a sh** load of money for a new exhaust system.  I said screw it and bought the Sprint manifolds from FS. and I grabbed the Borla system from Fiero Parts, the Accel Coil and the Accel performance module......ummmmmm also picked up a K&N airfilter and a pocket full of loose screws and bolts for the manifolds.  I finally made up mt mind after tear assin some Pimp mobile SUV.  Opened the hood when I got home and got a face full of hot air.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Carolina 88GT||02-19-2000||05:18 PM||||Oh yeah...and Im looking for a good free flow cat.   Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000011||turbo86se||02-20-2000||12:13 AM||||Carolina, ever make it down to Myrtle Beach? If so, give me a yell! Every once in a while I see an 84 or 85 coupe in Surfside with a ladder sticking out the passenger window. The owner does construction on some of the new beach homes or condos. <BR>I solved the hot air syndrome by modifying the manifolds. I had them ported and polished, and ceramic coated by Jet Hot. They look awesome! They really help out the Miller Woods turbo. <BR>A free-flow cat? Solved that too by removing it! A chunk had broken off inside and clogged the outlet when the engine was on. Probably the main reason why my front manifold cracked! LMK if you ever make it down to the beach!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Motorhead||02-20-2000||07:12 AM||||Hey, Turbo. I saw that car the day I bought my'86 in Surfside. White and winking.<BR>Have you seen the black and silver GT in Little River for sale?  Haven't stopped to check on it, but looks pretty good from the road.<BR>By the way, I live in Loris.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Carolina 88GT||02-20-2000||09:44 AM||||Turbo86se....Might very well make it down your way in a couple months...The little lady an I have been planning a get away from our little heathens. *ha  Will let you know||||reg||1
